{#
/**
 * @file
 * One retrieved source inside a panel's "Sources" list.
 *
 * Every source the assistant retrieved is listed, cited or not: what it had
 * available and declined to use is as diagnostic as what it quoted. The
 * comparison additionally marks the sources no other run retrieved.
 *
 * This is one item of a theme('item_list'), so it renders inline content with
 * no <li> of its own. Whitespace control is load-bearing throughout — item_list
 * puts this straight into the <li>, and a stray newline between the flag and
 * the badge would become a rendered space.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - link: The source title, as a link when it has an http(s) URL and as plain
 *   text otherwise. Built in PHP because the scheme allowlist is a decision,
 *   not markup.
 * - flag: Whether the source was cited, already translated.
 * - only_here: TRUE when no other run in this comparison retrieved this
 *   source. Always FALSE on the single-run page, which has nothing to be
 *   unique against.
 * - url: The source URL, shown under the title so a reader can see where a
 *   source came from without hovering. Empty when the source has none.
 */
#}
{{- link }} — <em>{{ flag }}</em>
{%- if only_here %}<span class="ys-compare-badge ys-compare-badge--only_here">{{ 'only in this run'|t }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if url %}<br><small>{{ url }}</small>{% endif -%}
